  "reply_text": "*Found one merge-blocking bug.*\n\n*P1 — View-only shares can edit unlocked documents* — `src/guard.js:12`\n\n`share.mask & WRITE === WRITE` is parsed as `share.mask & (WRITE === WRITE)`, so it tests bit `1` (`READ`), not bit `4` (`WRITE`).\n\nConfirmed:\n• A viewer with `READ` gets `canEdit(...) === true`.\n• A share with `WRITE` but no `READ` is incorrectly denied.\n\nUse `hasRight(share.mask, WRITE)` or parenthesize the bitwise expression before comparing. Add regression tests for a read-only viewer being denied editing and a write-only share being allowed on an unlocked document.\n\nAll six existing tests pass; they miss this because the tested editor has both READ and WRITE. I reviewed the full diff against `main` and found no other concrete bugs.\n\nNo code or files changed.",
